l", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment. "}]}], "template_override": 1}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn4le15ob07re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn4le15ob07re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn4le15ob07re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Tourist#1</span>: So, John? How far is Lima from where we anchored?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: It's about 25 miles, I believe. Lima sits on the cliffs over the sea, so we have to take the bus up to the city.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Tourist#1</span>: How long does that take? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: I'm not sure...maybe an hour.", "id": 1, "time": "1", "image": "engenn4le15ob07re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Tourist#1</span>: How far are the restaurants we are going to? From each other, I mean.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: I googled them and they look like they're a few miles from each other.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Tourist#1</span>: A few miles? My knees can't handle that, John!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: Well, we can take breaks between each place.", "id": 2, "time": "17000", "image": "engenn4le15ob07re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Tourist#2</span>:  I heard there's a Pisco Sour Day in Lima!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: Yes, they have a day to celebrate their cocktail.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Tourist#2</span>: Wow! When is that event?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: Hmm..I'm not sure. I can google that and get back to you.", "id": 3, "time": "33800", "image": "engenn4le15ob07re2img03.jpg"}]}}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "John in Peru"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "About Lima"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 15}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about directions to places in  a limited range of social situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "about "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "approximately"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's about 25 miles to Lima from here."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about walking tours."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to anchor"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to secure a ship in the water with an anchor"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We anchored 25 miles from Lima."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to sit "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be located"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The city sits on the cliffs over the sea."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cliff"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a steep rock near the sea"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We have to take a bus up the cliffs."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "I can't handle\u2026 "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "too much to deal with "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My knees can't handle the walk. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to take a break "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to take a rest"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We can take a break soon."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le15ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Saying How Far a Place Is"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the prepositions <span class=\"strong\">from </span> and <span class=\"strong\">to </span> when you want to talk about how far a place is. <br><br>  You use <span class=\"strong\">from </span> to talk about the starting point.  <br><br><span class=\"italic\">From our hotel, the park is 5 miles. </span> <br>or<br> <span class=\"italic\">The park is 5 miles from our hotel. </span><br><br> You use <span class=\"strong\">to </span> to talk about the ending point.<br>  <br>It is 5 miles to the park.  <br><br> To ask how far a place is, you use the phrase \u201cHow far\u2026?\u201d"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Anne</span>: How far is Lima from our boat? <br><span class=\"strong\">Michael</span>: It's about 25 miles to Lima."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Pisco Sour Day in Peru"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Pisco Sour is the Peruvian national cocktail (drink with alcohol). A Pisco sour is made of Pisco, lime juice, sugar, ice and whipped egg white. When you go to Peru as a tourist, you can try this refreshing drink. <br> <br>Peru celebrates Pisco Sour Day in February. There are music events, food stands and, of course, Pisco Sour!<br> <br> Do you want to try it?"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online and research a national day in another country."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 5-8 sentences about it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Give details like when it is and what you can do there."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Read your paragraph to your partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research about a national day in another country."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I locate information about its history and celebration."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a paragraph from my research information."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my paragraph to my partner."}]}], "type": "sena"}